// A model activation policy is an ordinary graph element. A successful
// observation commit already carries the store-attested identity of the exact
// trajectory prefix that contains it, so activation does not race a second
// State input. Instantiate this component once per independently wired fast,
// deliberative, or specialist model; routing remains outside the policy.
graph generation_policy {
    policy.GenerateOnObservation :: activation;
    input committed = activation.committed;
    input cancel = activation.cancel;
    output trigger = activation.trigger;
    // Wire this only when the model path may propose external effects. The
    // candidate names the exact observation basis selected by this policy.
    output authority = activation.authority;
    output state = activation.state;
    output outcome = activation.outcome;
}
